1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:03,445
Meet MXI RoboICL.

2
00:00:03,725 --> 00:00:07,200
Our team builds on learning through context, with geometry

3
00:00:07,200 --> 00:00:09,607
that helps robots act more precisely.

4
00:00:10,946 --> 00:00:12,765
Start with one demonstration.

5
00:00:13,058 --> 00:00:16,658
Short windows, sampled across time, show the model how the

6
00:00:16,658 --> 00:00:18,066
task unfolds.

7
00:00:18,358 --> 00:00:22,078
Each window connects what the robot sees, the actions taken,

8
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:23,566
and what happens next.

9
00:00:23,858 --> 00:00:26,528
The current episode follows the same format.

10
00:00:26,808 --> 00:00:30,420
Selected earlier interactions and the latest result join the

11
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,665
demonstration in the model’s context.

12
00:00:32,958 --> 00:00:36,140
The model decides, acts, and observes again.

13
00:00:36,433 --> 00:00:37,716
Its weights stay frozen.

14
00:00:38,008 --> 00:00:40,290
Experience changes the conversation.

15
00:00:44,958 --> 00:00:46,716
The robot sees the object.

16
00:00:46,996 --> 00:00:48,716
But where will its fingers close?

17
00:00:48,996 --> 00:00:51,478
Our wrist guides reveal the closing center.

18
00:00:51,758 --> 00:00:53,153
The camera is already there.

19
00:00:53,433 --> 00:00:56,640
We project the gripper geometry into its image.

20
00:00:56,908 --> 00:00:59,016
Watch the target approach the crosshair.

21
00:00:59,296 --> 00:00:59,916
Align.

22
00:01:00,208 --> 00:01:00,878
Close.

23
00:01:01,158 --> 00:01:01,666
Lift.

24
00:01:01,946 --> 00:01:06,433
Geometry makes the offset visible; the moving object reveals

25
00:01:06,433 --> 00:01:07,116
the result.

26
00:01:08,958 --> 00:01:12,166
A pixel tells us a direction, but not a distance.

27
00:01:12,446 --> 00:01:16,716
Now match the same vase opening in two calibrated camera views.

28
00:01:17,008 --> 00:01:19,053
Each observation defines a ray.

29
00:01:19,321 --> 00:01:23,208
Together, they constrain a three dimensional position, without

30
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:24,103
a depth map.

31
00:01:24,433 --> 00:01:27,778
Here, the reconstructed depth is about half a metre.

32
00:01:28,058 --> 00:01:31,090
The third view is occluded, so it is excluded.

33
00:01:31,383 --> 00:01:35,366
Back in the recorded rollout, the robot uses geometric information

34
00:01:35,458 --> 00:01:36,716
while adjusting the pour.

35
00:01:38,958 --> 00:01:40,941
A target is only the beginning.

36
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:43,340
The arm still needs a route it can execute.

37
00:01:43,658 --> 00:01:47,153
Here, the first preview fails inverse kinematics.

38
00:01:47,446 --> 00:01:48,628
No motion is sent.

39
00:01:48,908 --> 00:01:50,453
A revised plan passes.

40
00:01:50,733 --> 00:01:53,828
Now watch a translucent preview of the recorded arm motion:

41
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:58,016
approach, grasp, lift, transfer, and pour.

42
00:01:58,296 --> 00:02:00,466
Joint targets change along the route.

43
00:02:00,746 --> 00:02:04,658
This preview explains the accepted sequence; it is not a second

44
00:02:04,658 --> 00:02:05,803
physical robot.

45
00:02:06,083 --> 00:02:10,140
The overlay clears, and the recorded arm completes the task.

46
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:12,278
The episode scores one hundred.

47
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:20,966
MXI RoboICL keeps a compact foundation.

48
00:02:21,246 --> 00:02:25,028
The audited interface contains about six thousand characters.

49
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:29,696
Across three exploratory task groups, our system loses fewer

50
00:02:29,696 --> 00:02:33,466
points than Q0 when readable task information is removed.

51
00:02:33,746 --> 00:02:38,028
Our updated system reaches seventy-five point nine in team

52
00:02:38,208 --> 00:02:39,328
self-evaluation.

53
00:02:39,608 --> 00:02:43,903
These results motivate a simple direction: learn from experience,

54
00:02:44,158 --> 00:02:48,203
make geometry explicit, and check motion before execution.

55
00:03:12,862 --> 00:03:15,794
MXI RoboICL.

56
00:03:16,074 --> 00:03:18,232
An MXI team upgrade.

57
00:03:18,537 --> 00:03:19,394
Thank you for watching.
